error[O-Escapes]: this boundary carries an observation from an owner its signature does not permit
  --> tests/mem/discardability/a_discardable_child_handle_cannot_escape_its_owner.lin:11:5
   |
11 |     child.handle()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ escape observations only from the signature's declared sources
   |
   = help: part of the value comes from `outer`, which `where borrows(outer)` would permit; the rest no clause can
   = help: `child` is an allocator `child_handle` opens and ends, so nothing built in it may leave: take the allocator as a parameter instead, as `child_handle_in` with `A: Allocator` and `allocator: A` first, and build in `allocator`, so the caller's allocator decides how long the result lives
